From 5f6c03fa94876206e57eebd721e5aa9c318a6439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jarojarojaro-jaro <miki.jaroszek@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 17:05:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/70] HIP/RDNA3 FA: the kvq decode kernel also reads a q8_0
 KV cache (GGML_HIP_KVQ_Q8)

q8_0 K/V used to fall back to flash_attn_ext_vec, which fetches every K/V byte once per Q
head of a GQA group. The kvq kernel (RDNA3 WMMA, all Q heads of a KV head in one pass) now
has q8_0 instances for D 64 and 128 (D 256 spills registers there and stays on the vec kernel):
- K: q8_0 values to f16 via 0x6400|(q^0x80) - 1152 (exact), times d (one f16 rounding as q4_0),
- V: the same into the transposed f16 tile, the lane pair (r, r^2) exchanging the half blocks,
- half rows of an odd number of 34-byte blocks (D 64) start 2 bytes into a word: the lanes load
  whole words from the aligned word and select with a per-lane shift (rows must be 4-byte aligned),
- 1 block per WGP instead of 2 (in the model at 98k context: 129 us vs 147 us per call; 2 or 3
  blocks per WGP oversubscribe the memory with streams, unbalanced split counts cost more).

Numerics differ from the vec kernel (f16 Q and WMMA with f32 VKQ accumulators instead of q8_1 Q,
int8 dot products and f16 VKQ accumulators). KLD gate (LFM2.5-24B-A2B Q5_K_M, llama-perplexity
--kl-divergence, wikitext-2 test, 3 chunks of 16384 tokens, ubatch 1 = the decode kernels, vs
f16 KV of the same build): q8_0 vec kernel KLD 0.044171 +- 0.001726, same top p 92.248 %
(two runs bitwise identical); q8_0 kvq 0.044196 +- 0.001775, same top p 92.345 %, RMS dp 4.848 %
(vec 4.995 %), PPL ratio 1.0026 (vec 1.0138); q4_0 kvq 0.128359, same top p 85.215 %.

llama-bench tg128 -r 5, LFM2.5-24B-A2B, KV q8_0, 3 rounds interleaved, ms/token (off -> on):
depth 0 4.121 -> 4.099, 8192 4.290 -> 4.206, 32768 4.875 -> 4.526, 98304 6.561 -> 5.462 (+20 % t/s;
KV q4_0: 4.130 / 4.158 / 4.348 / 4.989). flash_attn per call at 98k: 223.5 us (vec) -> 129 us.
GGML_HIP_KVQ_Q8=0: the vec kernel. test-backend-ops: new q8_0 small-batch and LFM2-shape cases,
FLASH_ATTN_EXT 4060/4060.
